{#- The join page's mod section (scripts/plugins-section.py). A page cannot tell whether the moonpool: link
    has a handler, so a click says at once what should happen, and if the page still has focus a few seconds
    later, what to do when it didn't. Focus leaving pauses that wait (a window or prompt opened); coming back
    with nothing shown yet, such as after dismissing the browser's prompt, starts it again. A second click within
    two seconds of the first does nothing, so a double click does not start the launcher twice. -#}
{%- if launcher -%}
<a class="button" id="playmods" href="moonpool:{{ address }}">Play with mods</a>
{#- -#}
<div class="notice" id="opening" hidden><strong>Opening Moonpool&hellip;</strong> If your browser asks, allow it to open Moonpool. Its window lists the mods and asks before installing anything.</div>
{#- -#}
<div class="notice warn" id="nothing" hidden><strong>Still waiting?</strong> If your browser is asking to open Moonpool, allow it. If nothing is asking and no Moonpool window opened, this PC doesn't have the launcher yet. It takes a minute, once:
{#- -#}
<ol><li>Download the launcher with the button below. It is one small file from the Moonpool project on GitHub.</li>
{#- -#}
<li>Run it. Windows may say it protected your PC, because the file isn't code-signed: choose More info, then Run anyway.</li>
{#- -#}
<li>Press Play with mods again.</li></ol>
{#- -#}
<a class="button get" href="{{ setup_url }}">Download the launcher</a></div>
{#- -#}
<p>First time on this PC? <a href="{{ setup_url }}">Get the launcher</a> once, then press Play with mods.</p>
{#- -#}
<p class="fine">Play with mods installs or updates this server's mods and turns them on only until Subnautica 2 closes; normal launches don't load them. Mods run with your Windows account's rights, so only accept a host you trust.</p>
{#- -#}
<script>(function(){var b=document.getElementById("playmods"),o=document.getElementById("opening"),n=document.getElementById("nothing"),t=0;if(!b||!o||!n)return;function wait(){clearTimeout(t);t=setTimeout(function(){if(document.visibilityState==="visible"&&document.hasFocus()){o.hidden=true;n.hidden=false;}},4000);}var c=0;b.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(Date.now()-c<2000){e.preventDefault();return;}c=Date.now();b.style.opacity=".6";setTimeout(function(){b.style.opacity="";},2000);o.hidden=false;n.hidden=true;wait();});window.addEventListener("blur",function(){clearTimeout(t);});window.addEventListener("focus",function(){if(!o.hidden)wait();});})();</script>
{%- else -%}
<div class="opt"><p class="fine">Mods this server asks for:</p>
{%- endif -%}
<ul class="mods">
{%- for m in mods -%}
<li>{% if m.link %}<a href="{{ m.link }}">{{ m.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ m.name }}{% endif %}
{%- if m.version %} {{ m.version }}{% endif %}
{%- if m.notes %} ({{ m.notes|join(', ') }}){% endif %}
{%- if m.summary or m.stats %}<span class="about">{{ m.summary }}{% if m.summary and m.stats %}<br>{% endif %}
{%- if m.stats %}{% if m.stats.stars %}&#9733; {{ m.stats.stars }} on GitHub{% else %}{{ m.stats.downloads }} downloads on CurseForge{% endif %}
{%- if m.stats.updated %} &middot; updated {{ m.stats.updated }}{% endif %}
{%- if m.stats.by %} &middot; by {{ m.stats.by }}{% endif %}{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}</li>
{%- endfor -%}
</ul>
{%- if mods|selectattr('stats')|list %}<p class="fine">Stars and downloads come from GitHub and CurseForge. They show how widely a mod is used, not that its file is safe.</p>{% endif %}
{%- if not launcher %}</div>{% endif %}
